    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0295" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg215"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Lord Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2150.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In reply to your note No. 102, of
                    the 24th ultimo, I have the honor to inform you that it is stated in a letter of
                    the 6th instant from the Acting Secretary of the Navy that that Department has
                    had communication with Rear-Admiral Remy, and that it is now in a position to
                    say that the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn</hi> will visit New
                    Zealand after the completion of the ceremonies at Melbourne.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
